Yes. AI agents can use web search, but not by themselves. They need a web search tool or API that they can call.

Think of it this way:

🧠 LLM (Llama, GPT, Gemini) = Thinks and reasons.
🤖 Agent = Decides what action to take.
🔍 Web Search Tool = Searches the internet and returns information.

The agent chooses when to use the web search tool.

Example Workflow

User asks:

"Who won yesterday's IPL match?"

User
   │
   ▼
AI Agent
   │
   ▼
Web Search Tool
   │
(Searches Google/Bing/Brave)
   │
   ▼
Search Results
   │
   ▼
AI Agent
   │
   ▼
Final Answer

The agent first realizes it needs current information, calls the web search tool, then uses the results to answer.

